.el .ds Aq '
.TH xyrev-dotfile-decrypt 1  "xyrev-dotfile-decrypt "
.SH NAME
xyrev\-dotfile\-decrypt \- Decrypt a file using configured identities
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBxyrev\-dotfile\-decrypt\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-backend\fR] [\fB\-\-recipient\fR] [\fB\-\-identity\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decrypt a file using configured identities
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fR \fI<BACKEND>\fR

.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRage, gpg]
.TP
\fB\-\-recipient\fR \fI<RECIPIENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-identity\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\fR
Use age passphrase encryption; read the password privately from the terminal
.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read one passphrase line from a file or pipe (such as /dev/fd/3)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>

